<!--
    First real example of check#DeviceGroupNormCompliance (the DeviceGroup counterpart of
    CyberNormProductClassificationDemoSeedData.xml's PROD_SIE_XB208 example): applies all 7 IEC
    62443-3-3 FR requirement groups to both real Smoking Cell 1 panels
    (DG_PANEL_MSS311/DG_PANEL_QE1, CyberHvacCellDemoSeedData.xml) - any IACS zone is expected to
    address all 7 foundational requirement families, not a subset.

    Deliberately exercises both real outcomes of the one automatic evidence check that exists
    (SR 5.1/5.2 network segmentation, via DeviceGroupMemberPurpose=DgmpZoneBoundary):
    DG_PANEL_QE1 has a real DgmpZoneBoundary member (DEV_SW_MSS_1, the boundary switch to
    Corridor-1 - CyberHvacCellDemoSeedData.xml line 534) so its check should return SATISFIED;
    DG_PANEL_MSS311 has no such member, so its check should return MISSING - a genuine finding,
    not a fabricated negative (this panel's own switches were never modeled as a zone boundary,
    since the boundary in this real network is at the QE1 panel per the factory diagram).

    NOT auto-loaded (type="demo", same convention as CyberNormProductClassificationDemoSeedData.xml).
-->
